  "notes": "Basis: governmental funds are on a modified cash basis but presented as revenues/expenditures/fund balance, and the proprietary funds are accrual with a statement of cash flows, so basis = GAAP (fund balance roll-forward). Governmental lines use the Total column of the Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances (pages 21-24 of the report = trimmed pp 8-11). Loan Proceeds 7,684 is printed inside Total Revenue 497,438, so it is recorded in debt_proceeds (reported_totals.governmental.receipts includes debt_proceeds). Transfers: Total column shows transfers in 9,600 and out 0 (proprietary funds' 9,600 transfers out; the 42,400 eliminated in the Adjustments column). Roll-forward: 396,510 + 489,754 - 425,748 + 9,600 + 7,684 = 477,800. ending_cash = Cash and Cash Equivalents 442,402 on the governmental funds balance sheet total column (p7); Cash at County Treasurer 9,665 is a separate line. Business-type lines use the Totals column of the proprietary Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Fund Net Position (p16-17); business-type receipts/disbursements totals are sums of printed subtotals (see computed). Check: 2,224,598 + 1,203,081 - 1,114,547 - 9,600 = 2,303,532. Balance sheet is the government-wide Statement of Net Position Total column (pp1-2); balances. The Budgetary Comparison Schedule (pp20-21) is the main detail schedule; it is cash basis, total primary government, mixing governmental and business-type funds, and its actuals differ from the GAAP statements; its 'Other' local receipts line (1,298,608) includes utility receipts of the business-type funds and is tagged business-type with review. Fix pass (attempt 2): the budget schedule prints Transfers 52,000 (General 12,000 in + Street 40,000 in) with no transfer-out line; the outflows (General 40,000, Street 2,400 on p10, and Electric/Trash/Sewer/Water 2,400 each on p17 = 52,000 total) sit inside the spending lines on p21, so each was split into spending plus a signed other financing item (net other financing in detail = 0). The Trash/Sewer/Water splits are supported by p17 transfers (2,400) each and by the totals tying to 52,000, but their cash-basis line amounts cannot be tied to the cash flow statement. detail_totals expenditure 1,782,543 is as printed and includes the transfers out (includes other financing). Top-level transfers_in 9,600 / transfers_out 0 stay as the governmental funds statement Total column (42,400 eliminated in the Adjustments column). Detail 'State Receipts: Other' 13,254 recategorized to homestead/tax credits (equals Homestead 5,804 + Property Tax Credit 7,450). Re-trim (find_pages v8): gained the government-wide Statement of Activities (trimmed pp3-5; government-wide figures, nothing added since governmental receipts/disbursements come from the fund statement and tie: governmental net position 947,430, business-type 2,303,532), the Schedule of Expenditures - Modified Cash Basis - Governmental Funds (p22, funds x object, total 425,748) and the Electric statistical data schedule (p23, unaudited, KWH data; nothing added). The p22 schedule is more detailed than the budget schedule's four governmental function lines (General Government 151,655 + Public Safety 436 + Public Works 195,014 + Culture and Recreation 78,643 = 425,748, after the hidden transfer splits), so those four lines were replaced by its object lines (fund column in department; General/City Hall = general government incl. public safety 436, Street and Alley = streets/highways, Park/Pool = culture/recreation; Grants Fund all zero); the budget schedule's printed expenditure total 1,782,543 ties via includes_schedules, and its governmental budget_final figures (160,000 / 10,000 / 251,200 / 130,000) are no longer carried. Read pages 1-23 of 23.",
